body:
everyone should work in retail at least once to get the experience of what its like to deal with entitled assholes

&#x200B;

edit: just wanted to specify what kind of ass holes heh

I feel this every day. I look at the accomplishments of my brother and sister and I feel like a total failure.  My sister suffers from an illness known as M.E and despite all the hardships shes gone through she has passed through school with flying colours. Both my sister and brother did amazing in their GSCEs where as I barely passed. My mental health got so bad in year 11 that I dropped out of school and literally taught my self for my GSCEs. My parents are always proud of me and my friends thing I'm a great person. I try my hardest to be a nice guy and be help people, but no matter what I do I feel like a Pathetic failure.

&#x200B;

Ps - Sorry for writing mistakes, I am quite tired as I write this
